===================== Version1.1.17 =====================
Version: 1.1.17
Date:    2023-08-22
Author:  xiaolong zhang
Email:   zhangxiaolong@big.ac.cn
Descrip:
    1. file_read.c/file_name_copy: fix the 'malloc(): memory corruption'. This bug is introduced by error access to memory
       that not allocated! 
       Note: if the given 'str' is not end with '\r' or '\n', the 'idx' will be equal to l_str, so dest_str[idx] will exceed
             the real memory allocated to dest_str.


===================== Version1.1.18 =====================
Version: 1.1.18
Date:    2023-09-04
Author:  xiaolong zhang
Email:   zhangxiaolong@big.ac.cn
Descrip:
    since the most of the ERROR:014 are induced by "failed to detect line breaks('\n')", therefore, add the line breaker detection
    1. file_read.c/gz_read_util: when ks_str->m > max_len, return -2 to tell the user that
    the issue is mainly due to the line breaks of the read
    2. fastq_check.c/fastq_cache_read: store the error introduced by the too long read (rare)
    or failed to detect line breaks (mainly)


===================== Version1.1.19 =====================
Version: 1.1.19
Date:    2023-10-05
Author:  xiaolong zhang
Email:   zhangxiaolong@big.ac.cn
Descrip:
    some of the fastq file has a very high compression ratio, so that underestimated the size of the bloomfilter
    1. params_parse.c: add parameter -r|--ratio, which allow user to specify the compression ratio of the input fastq file
    2. fastq_check.c/bloomfilter_size_init: add parameter of compress_ratio


===================== Version1.1.20 =====================
Version: 1.1.20
Date:    2024-02-20
Author:  xiaolong zhang
Email:   zhangxiaolong@big.ac.cn
Descrip:
    some of the fastq file from BGISEQ-2000 and MGISEQ-2000 have a special pair_marker:
    e.g. "@HWI-ST833:189:5:2200#0/2" or "@HWI-ST833:189:5:2200#0/2\t5\t1"
    modify both get_first_read_marker and read_name_trim with isspace(ctype.h) to process such conditions


===================== Version1.1.21 =====================
Version: 1.1.21
Date:    2024-04-26
Author:  xiaolong zhang
Email:   zhangxiaolong@big.ac.cn
Descrip:
    modify the GZ_BUFF_SIZE and add a function of gzbuffer to increase IO throughput
    1. file_read.h: set GZ_BUFF_SIZE to 4MB
    2. file_read.c: set gzbuffer to 128MB (default 8K)


===================== Version2.0.0 =====================
Version: 2.0.0
Date:    2026-08-14
Author:  xiaolong zhang
Email:   zhangxiaolong@big.ac.cn
Descrip:
    redesign the check flow as a multithreading pipeline to speed up the checking of large-scale fastq files
    1. fastq_check.c: add the multithreading pipeline (a reader thread + a reader threadpool with one thread for each input file)
       a checker threadpool with n_thread threads for the batch content checking;
       a duplicate-check thread for the read name checking;
    2. kqueue.c/kqueue.h: add the thread-safe circular queue (kqueue) as the task queue between the reader thread and the duplicate-check thread
    3. fastq_check.c: add the thread task object (thread_task_t) with the batch status mask protocol (1: batch cached -> 11: content checked -> 111: duplicate checked)
    4. params_parse.c: add the -t|--thread parameter to set the number of threads used when checking (default: 1)
    5. bloom_filter.c/bloom_filter.h: split the source code and header file (v1.3) and add BloomFilterCheckAdd (double hashing) for the multithread duplicate checking
    6. fastq_check.c: fix the data loss bug at the end of the file (the last partial batch was dropped by mistake)
    7. fastq_check.c: fix the deadlock bug caused by the task status mask (the batch was popped from the queue before all files of the batch were cached)
    8. fastq_check.c: fix the base count over-count bug in the multithread mode (the running cumulative sum was accumulated repeatedly)
    